Local patch for NVIDIA SkillEvaluator v0.6.0 (applied by runner/Dockerfile with `patch -p1`).
Regenerate: fetch src/skillevaluator/cli.py, src/skillevaluator/tier3/harbor/runner.py and
src/skillevaluator/tier3/harbor/local_agents.py at tag v0.6.0, edit, then `diff -u a/<file> b/<file>`.
Each hunk, by file:

cli.py
  1. `validate --catalog FILE` (option): a saved Tier 2 catalog (`similarity-check --save-catalog`).
     Without it validate compares the skill only with itself, so a skill that duplicates another
     skill in the registry would pass Tier 2.
  2. `validate` signature: receives the new `catalog` parameter.
  3. `validate` Tier 2 stage: after the intra-skill dedup, runs the same inter-skill
     similarity check as `skillevaluator tier2 --catalog` (threshold 0.75) and folds its results
     into Tier 2, so one `validate` run covers Tier 1, Tier 2 (with catalog) and Tier 3 and the
     publication assessment of its report is complete.

tier3/harbor/runner.py
  4. Environment allowlist for `--env-mode ack`: lets HARBOR_SANDBOX_IMAGE (the prebuilt sandbox
     image that replaces per-task image builds), HARBOR_SANDBOX_CPUS and HARBOR_SANDBOX_MEMORY_MB
     (sandbox size), HARBOR_SANDBOX_WARM_POOL (the SandboxWarmPool of the eval's sandbox
     profile: trials claim their pods from it) and SKILLEVAL_NAME (the trial pod label the
     eval's network policy selects) reach Harbor, where
     harbor_agent_sandbox.AgentSandboxEnvironment reads them. HARBOR_BUILDKIT_ADDRESS (a BuildKit
     of your own, for the optional image build) goes through too. `validate` has no
     --override-cpus/--override-memory-mb, so the size travels in the environment.
  5. Command builder: SKILLEVALUATOR_ACK_ENV_IMPORT_PATH replaces the `ack` environment type with
     an import path, e.g. harbor_agent_sandbox:AgentSandboxEnvironment (Agent Sandbox instead of
     bare pods).
  6. New `_GATEWAY_OPENCODE_IMPORT_PATH` and `_opencode_gateway()`: true when
     SKILLEVALUATOR_OPENCODE_GATEWAY=1. Hunks 8 to 11 read it. The wrapper joins
     `_NATIVE_BACKEND_AGENT_IMPORT_PATHS` next to the gateway Codex wrapper; without that the
     command builder refuses any agent import path outside docker, kata and local, and Tier 3
     of an OpenCode gateway run is skipped on `ack`.
  7. `_harbor_agent_kwargs` (agent version): SKILLEVALUATOR_AGENT_VERSION replaces the pinned
     `version` kwarg of the selected agent (claude-code 2.1.292, codex 0.161.0) and sets one for
     OpenCode, which upstream leaves unpinned (Harbor then installs the latest release in every
     trial). Ignored in local mode. The variable is read in-process by SkillEvaluator, so the Harbor
     environment allowlist does not matter. Without the variable nothing changes.
  8. `_validate_agent_provider_credentials`: with the gateway flag, an OpenCode model like
     `openai/gpt-oss:120b` no longer has to carry the evaluator provider (anthropic) as prefix.
  9. `_agent_credentials`: with the Anthropic evaluator and the gateway flag, OpenCode receives
     OPENAI_API_KEY and OPENAI_BASE_URL (the operator's OpenAI-compatible gateway) instead of the
     Anthropic key, exactly as Codex does. The judge stays on the evaluator provider.
 10. `_agent_provider_config`: describes that OpenCode route as an OpenAI-compatible provider, so
     the credential and catalog check asks the gateway (OPENAI_BASE_URL/models) about the model.
 11. `_agent_import_path`: with the gateway flag, OpenCode runs as SkillEvaluatorGatewayOpenCode
     (Chat Completions through @ai-sdk/openai-compatible; OpenCode's built-in openai provider
     always uses the Responses API).

tier3/harbor/local_agents.py
 12. `SkillEvaluatorGatewayOpenCode.model_connection`: forwards OPENAI_API_KEY to the agent.
     The wrapper renames the model to `skillevaluator-gateway/<id>`, a provider Harbor does not
     know, so Harbor resolved no key for it and the provider config's `{env:OPENAI_API_KEY}` was
     empty in the sandbox: every OpenCode trial through a gateway failed with HTTP 401.

tier3/harbor/runner.py (added after hunk 12, sits between hunks 5 and 8 in the file)
 13. Command builder (trial retries): SKILLEVALUATOR_TRIAL_RETRIES=N (N > 0) adds
     `--max-retries N --retry-include ApiRateLimitError`, so Harbor runs a trial again, with
     the same name, when the agent hit a provider rate limit. SKILLEVALUATOR_HARBOR_CONFIG adds
     `-c <file>`: a JobConfig file with only `retry:` that sets the backoff (wait_multiplier,
     min_wait_sec, max_wait_sec), which has no CLI flag. Harbor loads the file first and applies
     every flag over it, so it changes nothing else. Both variables are read in-process; without
     them, or with N=0, the command is unchanged.

